# Caddy in front of the share server: it gets and renews the certificate for the name by itself.
# The name must point at the machine (an A record), and ports 80 and 443 must be open.
# Events (what keeps readers' pages live) pass through as they come; Caddy flushes event streams on its own.
share.example.org {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
